WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.500
Your customers now ask AI what to buy.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:09.720
So Poliris asks AI the same questions,
every week, and reads every answer.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.870
Good news: in the US, you
show up in 64% of answers.

4
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.290
And you can see where you stand
in every other trading zone.

5
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.050
But ask about the
performance of your battery,

6
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.260
and you're cited in just
2 answers out of 9.

7
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:29.320
Worse, when AI does bring it up, it
rates you below your competitors.

8
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:30.680
And on Google?

9
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.700
Same story: you don't rank
on a single battery search.

10
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.690
Star those searches, and
Poliris tracks them every week.

11
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.580
Why?

12
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.540
The answer is on your website.

13
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.500
Poliris checks if AI can reach your
pages, read them, and trust them.

14
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:50.500
Every page is crawled and
put through 150 tests.

15
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:55.870
Your battery page scores just
45: no FAQ, no product data.

16
00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.030
AI can barely read it.

17
00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:04.420
So you ask Nora, your GEO analyst, for a
plan to win back those battery answers.

18
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:10.100
She cross-checks your AI answers, your
keywords and your site, and writes the plan.

19
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.820
Export it as a report for your team.

20
00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.850
Or apply it, and your roadmap
updates, with a task for each agent.

21
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:24.550
Every task lands in its lane:
technical fixes, content, or citations.

22
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:30.280
Launch the battery guide, and Kate, your
content agent, takes it from there.

23
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.060
She writes it from the brief, scores
it, and it's ready to publish.

24
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:39.630
Meanwhile, Tom prepares the code
fixes for your battery page,

25
00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.620
ready for your developers.

26
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.400
And Nora gets you cited
by the sites AI trusts:

27
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:51.080
ask for a link, claim a listing, or buy
a placement, all without leaving Poliris.

28
00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:58.390
At the next analysis, you show up in 78%
of answers, and you lead your market.

29
00:01:58.550 --> 00:01:59.460
Poliris.

30
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.990
The Search Intelligence Platform.
